
==============================================================================
1. Letter level: carrying a qubit letter to the qutrit through a read link (exact)
==============================================================================
(A (x) 1)|omega_2> = (1 (x) B)|omega_2>  <=>  A = [[b0, b2, a2], [b1, b3, a5], [0, 0, a8]]
  i.e. A = B^T on S = span{|0>,|1>}, zero from S into |2>; the column of |2> (a2, a5, a8) is not fixed by the link
B traceless Hermitian, A required traceless Hermitian: unique solution A = t(B) = iota B^T iota^dag = [[z, x + I*y, 0], [x - I*y, -z, 0], [0, 0, 0]]
B = 1, A Hermitian: A = [[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, a8]]  -> the value b = a8 at the third direction is free (b = 0: support
  projector, what the link itself gives; b = 1: identity)
  t(sigma_x) = +lambda_1;  PS t PS = t: True;  t |2> = 0: True
  t(sigma_y) = -lambda_2;  PS t PS = t: True;  t |2> = 0: True
  t(sigma_z) = +lambda_3;  PS t PS = t: True;  t |2> = 0: True
  so the transported qubit letters are the Gell-Mann letters lambda_1, -lambda_2, lambda_3 of the su(2) on S

Lie algebra of the subgroup H of G_Omega = SU(3) x SU(2) fixing both read links P_L1, P_L2: dim 4
  projection of h onto su(2)_q has rank 3 ; every element has U|_S = c Vbar and U|2> in C|2> (residual 1.6e-16); the kernel of the projection (1-dim) is lambda_8 at the qutrit (defect 1.9e-16)
  so H = {(U, V): U = c Vbar (+) c^-2} = SU(2) x U(1), the diagonal su(2) on S plus lambda_8 (cf. Supplement S3, Thm S-stabilizer)
  E' exchanges the two read links: ||E'(P_L1) - P_L2|| = 0.0e+00
  commutant on C^3 of h: 2 (span{PS, |2><2|}: invariant subspaces 0, S, C|2>, C^3);  of su(3): 1 (invariant subspaces 0, C^3)
equivariant maps qubit letters -> qutrit letters: under G_Omega 0 (Schur: (1,3) -> (8,1)), under H 1; t spans the H-equivariant ones: True
  => the transport is, up to scale, the only H-equivariant one, and no nonzero transport is G_Omega-equivariant

