==============================================================================
SUMMARY
==============================================================================
1. The transport of a qubit letter through its read link is unique (t(B) = iota B^T iota^dag), lives on the 2-dim
   support S, is H-equivariant (H = SU(2) x U(1), dim 4) and has no nonzero G_Omega-equivariant version.
2. Uniform transport (every record) is many-to-one on R: odd cross-mixed records collide with odd QQ records (kappa = 2/3,
   M_L and K_L need 1), even cross-mixed with even QQ, and commutator with odd same-link mixed records (Rayleigh quotients
   forced equal, the Letter has sqrt2 vs sqrt3 and sqrt6 vs 1). So no D in the transported frame, as T^+ D T or as
   Rayleigh quotients, gives M_L or K_L, for any of the six transports.
3. F3 (338688 ordered choices): M_L is reached by 6 choices, all with the credit J1 = sqrt3 and with X in the
   transported frame and Y in the original frame (qubit end). With the H-invariant credits the Letter-shaped member gives
   J2: 79+48r2+40r3+2r6  1/value 140.702
   J3: 85+54r2+36r3  1/value 139.030
4. F3a (5953 distinct compressions with a transport letter): no class-scalar or class-constant word at all, so none
   reproduces sqrt(k_r) or k_r as operator or diagonal; per-isotypic traces: best residual 0.0947 (identity 0.2070, F1 best 0.1008).
